# DI-06-01: stop the MAIN Nx graph from discovering the matrix-e2e consumer-workspace
# fixture's nested projects (apps/app, libs/{local-lib,buildable-lib,publishable-lib}).
#
# Those fixtures are an INSTALLED-consumer workspace exercised ONLY from inside the
# angular-typechecker-matrix-e2e spec (which copies them to a per-run tmp dir, installs
# the packed tarball, and runs the executor by its PUBLISHED id). They must NOT be
# members of THIS repo's project graph: the buildable-lib/publishable-lib declare
# @nx/angular:ng-packagr-lite / :package build targets WITHOUT ng-packagr installed
# (OQ-1 -- the executor never RUNS the build, only reads tsConfig), so an unscoped
# `nx run-many -t build` (e.g. the release preVersionCommand) sweeps them in and fails
# with "Cannot find module 'ng-packagr'".
#
# This excludes ONLY the fixtures subdir -- the angular-typechecker-matrix-e2e project
# itself (its `test` target) stays in the graph.
e2e/angular-typechecker-matrix-e2e/fixtures/

# 19-02: stop the MAIN Nx graph from discovering the Storybook Composition fixture's
# THREE projects (lib-buttons, lib-cards, storybook-host).
#
# Same rationale as the matrix-e2e block above: this is a multi-project consumer
# workspace exercised ONLY from inside the angular-typechecker-install-e2e spec
# (storybook-composition.e2e.spec.ts copies it to a per-run tmp dir and runs the
# executor by its PUBLISHED id). It must NOT be a member of THIS repo's graph for TWO
# reasons: (1) its `storybook-host` project name COLLIDES with consumer-storybook-b's
# `storybook-host` (nx errors: "projects defined in multiple locations"); and (2) each
# composed lib PRE-COMMITS an `angular-typechecker:typecheck` target (the Composition
# topology needs them committed, not generated at test time), so an unscoped
# `nx run-many -t typecheck` in the dev workspace would sweep them in with dev-root
# tsConfig paths that do not resolve. The tmp-copied workspace has no such collision
# and still discovers all three projects.
e2e/angular-typechecker-install-e2e/fixtures/consumer-storybook-composition/
